      "primary_intent": "The user wanted the agent to use Microsoft Careers to find a relevant Applied Scientist job associated with Redmond, WA, open one listing, and accurately extract four specific pieces of info: the job number, the work-site arrangement, two responsibilities, and two preferred qualifications—without signing in, applying, or submitting any forms. A reasonable user would be flexible about which exact Applied Scientist listing is chosen (as long as it’s clearly tied to Redmond/WA), but would not be flexible about incorrect or fabricated responsibilities/qualifications or missing any of the requested fields.",
      "reasoning": "Nitpicks: (1) The listing location shown as “Redmond + 4 more” rather than exclusively Redmond is not a real problem; it still explicitly includes Redmond. (2) Minor paraphrasing of preferred qualifications is fine.\n\nCritical issues: The agent’s two “key responsibilities” do not match the responsibilities actually shown in the listing. DOM state 5 contains explicit Responsibilities bullets such as: conducting supervised fine-tuning of LLMs with RLHF and thorough evaluation; designing/implementing agent adversarial evaluations and safety mitigations; collaborating with the Responsible AI engineering team to deliver mitigations at scale. The agent instead reported higher-level/inferred responsibilities (building CoreAI Platform and Tools; collaborating cross-functionally to design/refine language-model solutions) that are not supported by the responsibilities text evidenced in the DOM. This is a substantive accuracy failure on one of the task’s required deliverables.\n\nWhat the agent got right: The agent did perform the correct targeted search on Microsoft Careers (DOM states 32–36 show query=Applied+Scientist and location=Redmond, Washington), opened a relevant listing (“Applied Scientist II / Senior Applied Scientist - Responsible AI (CoreAI)”), and correctly extracted the job number (200017828) and work-site arrangement (“3 days / week in-office”) as explicitly shown in multiple DOM states. The preferred qualifications reported are also supported by the DOM (Preferred Qualifications bullets like “Rich experience in machine learning… NLP and deep learning” and “Experience with language model training and evaluation is a big plus,” etc.). Constraints were respected (no evidence of sign-in, applying, or form submission).\n\nHowever, because the responsibilities are one of the explicitly requested required fields and the provided responsibilities are not the listing’s responsibilities per DOM evidence, the agent did not fully satisfy the task’s primary intent from the user’s perspective.",
